  "reason": "RNA with scvi_n200 is the strongest direction so far, with multiprofile avgpool/transformer reaching about 0.65 accuracy and 0.63 F1, but single-profile scvi is untested. Multiprofile helped PCA and ResNet image baselines, yet we should not assume it is necessary for scvi. This experiment tests whether a simpler single-profile scvi model can match the multiprofile scvi results, clarifying the importance of profile/aggregation for the best RNA encoder. It is a high-value next step because it extends the most promising unimodal model, has high expected accuracy, and reduces uncertainty before adding multimodal fusion complexity."
